solution_steps:
We want to find the value of $X$ in the given situation.
We are given three equations:
\begin{align*}
x + yz &= X, \\
y + xz &= 10, \\
z + xy &= 10.
\end{align*}
To find the value of $X$, we can solve these equations simultaneously.
We can start by subtracting the second and third equations from the first equation:
\begin{align*}
(x + yz) - (y + xz) &= X - 10, \\
(x + yz) - (z + xy) &= X - 10.
\end{align*}
Simplifying these equations gives us:
\begin{align*}
x - y - xz + yz &= X - 10, \\
x - z + yz - xy &= X - 10.
\end{align*}
Factoring out $z$ from the first equation and factoring out $y$ from the second equation, we have:
\begin{align*}
z(x - y) + y(x - z) &= X - 10, \\
y(z - x) + x(z - y) &= X - 10.
\end{align*}
Rearranging these equations gives us:
\begin{align*}
z(x - y) &= X - 10 - y(x - z), \\
y(z - x) &= X - 10 - x(z - y).
\end{align*}
Now, we can divide both sides of these equations by $(x - y)$ and $(z - x)$, respectively:
\begin{align*}
z &= \frac{X - 10 - y(x - z)}{x - y}, \\
y &= \frac{X - 10 - x(z - y)}{z - x}.
\end{align*}
Given that the value of $x_1 + x_2 + \dots + x_n$ is 7, we can substitute it into the equation:
$7 = x_1 + x_2 + \dots + x_n$
Now, we have:
$7 = x_1 + x_2 + \dots + x_n$
The value of $X$ is 7.
The answer is: 7

